{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And he loved also Rachel</b>: Scripture mentions that he also loved Rachel more than Leah. The reason is that by nature one tends to love more the woman whom a man knew first, as the Sages stated concerning women (Sanhedrin 22a) — she forms a bond only with the one who made her into a vessel. Yet Jacob loved Rachel more than Leah, contrary to the usual way of the world, and this is the force of \"also\"."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:28.424776516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}